  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Thesis Ledger",
    "overview": "SiTA is a record of where each thesis stands, so the interface reads like a well-kept ledger: pale surfaces, hairline borders, one blue, and status colour that means the same thing on every page. It is calm on purpose. A student on a phone and a lecturer on a laptop both need to find the next step in a few seconds, and nothing decorative should compete with that.\n\nThe system is the shadcn/ui stack (Radix primitives, `cva` variants, Tailwind v4 tokens) with a domain layer on top: shared page patterns in `resources/js/components/patterns/` and semantic status tokens in `resources/css/app.css`. Pages compose those patterns and tokens. They do not hand-roll status colours or redeclare the patterns. The Filament admin panel at `/admin` is a separate surface that is kept visually paired with the React tokens (see Components).\n\nThis file records the incumbent system as it is built, plus the rules that were carried over from the former standalone design-system doc. Where the build drifts from a rule, the rule stands and the drift is listed under Do's and Don'ts as known drift. Product facts (users, tone, brand) live in `PRODUCT.md`.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One brand colour (UBG Blue) with a light and a dark theme; UBG Blue is the only theme that meets WCAG AA.",
      "Semantic status roles (primary, success, warning, danger, info, muted), each defined as four tokens in both themes.",
      "Tonal layering with hairline borders; a single soft shadow on cards, larger shadows only on floating layers.",
      "Sentence-case Indonesian labels, 12px minimum, one sans family.",
      "Phone-first for mahasiswa, laptop-first for dosen, kaprodi and admin."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Default Theme Rule",
        "body": "UBG Blue (light and dark) is the default theme and the only one that meets WCAG AA. `resources/js/hooks/use-primary-color.ts` writes the selected preset inline on `<html>`, overriding `app.css`, so its `ubg-blue` entry must carry the same values as `:root`/`.dark`. The other presets (emerald, sunset, rose, indigo, teal) are proof-of-concept and fail AA in light and dark; accessible schemes defined as CSS tokens are tracked in #50.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Light Primary In Dark Rule",
        "body": "Primary is `#2563eb` with white text in light mode, and `#60a5fa` with dark (`#0f172a`) text in dark mode. Dark primary is light on purpose: `text-primary` (links, active states, icons) must stay readable on dark surfaces, and the dark status solids follow the same light-fill/dark-text rule.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tint Pair Rule",
        "body": "Text on a primary tint uses `bg-primary-muted text-primary-muted-foreground` (active navigation, avatar initials, soft badges and buttons, icon chips). `bg-primary/10 text-primary` measures about 4.5:1 or less in light mode and fails AA once the tint is stronger or the base is not white.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Foreground Pairing Rule",
        "body": "Text on `bg-primary` uses `text-primary-foreground`; a count chip nested in a primary pill is inverted (`bg-primary-foreground text-primary`). Never `text-white`/`bg-white/20` on primary (dark primary is light), and no translucent `primary-foreground/20` chip under white text (it lightens the fill below 4.5:1). In general, pair solid fills with `-foreground`, and muted surfaces with `-muted-foreground`. Browser-resolved sRGB measurements for the 16 success/warning/danger/info light/dark pairs were at least 5.07:1. Recheck contrast when changing values or introducing new combinations.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Muted Badge Rule",
        "body": "Badges and callouts use the muted surface with its `-muted-foreground` text (`bg-success-muted text-success-muted-foreground`). Solid fills (`bg-danger text-danger-foreground`) are for emphasis such as alerts and buttons.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paired Palettes Rule",
        "body": "The Filament admin cannot load the React stylesheet, so its palettes mirror these tokens. See Components, Filament admin.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Labels are Indonesian, sentence case, at least `text-xs` (12px). Avoid `text-[9px]`/`text-[10px]` and uppercase `tracking-widest` micro-labels for content; use `text-xs font-medium text-muted-foreground`.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Numbers Rule",
        "body": "Numbers that stand alone as plain text use `tabular-nums`; they are not wrapped in a pill (see Composition rules).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Surface Rule",
        "body": "A `SectionCard`/`Card` already has border and shadow; content inside it uses borders or dividers, not another shadowed card. `DataTableContainer` has a border but no shadow for that reason, and a page must not add `shadow-sm` to a `Card` (it is the default).",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
